<para>Screen 2 - Using the given table, Hannah's price is validated as the best price. Explain why the store worker thinks
  the total for 13 bagels should cost $16.25.</para>
<para>Use the sentence stem: <emphasis>The store worker thinks the price for 13 bagels should be $16.25 because …</emphasis></para>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>The store worker thinks the price for 13 bagels should be $16.25 because she multiplied 13
  times 1.25. She charged the customer for each bagel individually. </para>
<para>Screen 3 - Using the given table, Hannah's price is validated as the best price. Explain why Jaime thinks the total
  for 13 bagels should cost $13.25.</para>
<para>Use the sentence stem: <emphasis>Jaime thinks the price for 13 bagels should be $13.25 because …</emphasis></para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Jaime thinks the price for 13 bagels should be $13.25 because that is the cost of buying two
  sets of six bagels and then one more bagel.</para>
<para>Screen 4 - Using the given table, Hannah's price is validated as the best price. Explain why Pedro thinks the total
  for 13 bagels should cost $13.00.</para>
<para>Use the sentence stem: <emphasis>Pedro thinks the price for 13 bagels should be $13.00 because …</emphasis></para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Pedro thinks the price for 13 bagels should be $13.00 because he added the costs of buying
  10 bagels and then 3 more bagels. </para>
<para>Screen 5, Question 1 - Pretend you are the owner of the bagel shop. Explain why you would create a price list like
  this.</para>
<para>Use the sentence stem: <emphasis>A price list like this benefits the owner because ...</emphasis></para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Your answer may vary, but here are some samples:</para>
<list>
  <item>A price list like this benefits the owner because it encourages customers to buy more bagels since they will think
    they may be getting a better deal. </item>
  <item>A price list like this benefits the owner because it rewards customers who buy larger quantities with cheaper
    prices. </item>
</list>
<para>Screen 5, Question 2 - Pretend you are the customer who is buying the 13 bagels. Explain if you like for items to be
  priced like this and why.</para>
<para>Use one of the sentence stems: <emphasis>I do not like price lists like this because …</emphasis> OR <emphasis>I do not mind price
    lists like this because ...</emphasis> </para>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Your answer may vary, but here are some sample examples:</para>
<list>
  <item>I do not like price lists like this because it would be easy to be overcharged for my purchases. </item>
  <item>I do not mind price lists like this because I can get a better deal for 12 bagels compared to buying them at the
    individual price. </item>
</list>
